  {
   "mark": "hall_door",
   "id": "hall_dead",
   "if_flag": "dannotalos_dead",
   "say": "Dannotalos's hall is shut up and the hearth is cold. His men have carried him home to his own people for the burning, and taken his horses with them. Nobody has swept the floor."
  },
  {
   "mark": "epo",
   "id": "epo_seen",
   "unless_flag": "gergovia_besieged",
   "say": "A knot of riders goes by at a walk, young men with gold at their throats and Roman saddles, and the street makes room for them. The one in front is Eporedorix, someone says: a noble's son, the best horseman of the Aedui, and Caesar's friend. He doesn't look at anybody."
  },
  {
   "mark": "council_altar",
   "id": "council_view",
   "say": "The council ground is a square of beaten earth inside a ditch and a fence, with an altar in the middle of it, black from old fires. This is where the Aedui choose their vergobret, through the priests, and where they'll decide, sooner or later, whose war this is."
  }
